  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Australian politics live: Taylor says Hanson should delete One Nation ‘traitor’ cartoon; Moira Deeming joins Family First",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/10/anthony-albanese-labor-uk-west-bank-trade-ban-kevin-rudd-diplomacy-one-nation-pauline-hanson-liberal-party-angus-taylor-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow the day’s news live</p><p><strong>Labor introducing new laws to crack down on illegal tobacco</strong></p><p>Labor will introduce new laws to make it easier to prosecute criminals involved in the illicit tobacco trade, as the government fights an uphill battle against the exploding black market.</p><p>The new laws think about it as a list of observable indicators, very simple, fact-based things like: is the tobacco appropriately packaged? Is it a menthol cigarette even hiding in plain packaging? Is it being concealed? Does it have paperwork at the border?</p><p>Or my personal favourite: is the retail price of this packet of cigarettes less than the amount of excise and GST combined? If any of these facts are proven, just one of them, that establishes the reasonable suspicion of the criminal offence of importing, possession, or conveying. It’ll give powerful new tools to Border Force but every state and territory police force to go after the crooks.</p><p>I said, look, my door’s open if you want to talk about this. I don’t know why he thinks I’m a liar. I don’t quite know why he believes I lied about it.</p><p>I’m disappointed he thinks I’m a coward. I don’t know how he came to that opinion but that’s up to him. I don’t think he’s a traitor. I absolutely respect the services given to our nation, like my family, has given to the service of New Zealand and Australia. Democracy’s a robust thing.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/10/anthony-albanese-labor-uk-west-bank-trade-ban-kevin-rudd-diplomacy-one-nation-pauline-hanson-liberal-party-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-10T01:38:53"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jacqui Lambie says Pauline Hanson a ‘bloody coward’ after One Nation cartoon calling Andrew Hastie a traitor",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/10/jacqui-lambie-says-pauline-hanson-a-bloody-coward-after-one-nation-cartoon-calling-andrew-hastie-a-traitor-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Lambie, a veteran and Tasmanian senator, says One Nation leader is showing her ‘true colours’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/10/anthony-albanese-labor-uk-west-bank-trade-ban-kevin-rudd-diplomacy-one-nation-pauline-hanson-liberal-party-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Jacqui Lambie has accused Pauline Hanson of being a “coward” for a One Nation cartoon calling the<strong> </strong>Liberal frontbencher Andrew Hastie a traitor, amid a growing spat between the One Nation leader and the former SAS captain.</p><p>Lambie, a veteran and Tasmanian senator, defended Hastie on Thursday, after he called on Hanson to take ownership for a One Nation animated cartoon on social media in which he is repeatedly described as a traitor for giving evidence against Victoria Cross recipient Ben Roberts-Smith in his failed defamation case.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/10/jacqui-lambie-says-pauline-hanson-a-bloody-coward-after-one-nation-cartoon-calling-andrew-hastie-a-traitor-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-10T01:29:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "Victoria’s koalas in chronically poor health and population is half what was previously estimated",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/10/victorias-koalas-in-chronically-poor-health-and-population-is-half-what-was-previously-estimated",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> State government delayed releasing major report into the health of the koala population for more than 12 months</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/10/anthony-albanese-labor-uk-west-bank-trade-ban-kevin-rudd-diplomacy-one-nation-pauline-hanson-liberal-party-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Victorian government sat on a report for more than 12 months that found the state’s koala population was in chronically poor health.</p><p>The <a href=\"https://www.parliament.vic.gov.au/4a56eb/globalassets/tabled-paper-documents/tabled-paper-10478/koala-status-ari-technical-report-final.pdf\">review</a> of the state’s koala populations, led by state science agency the Arthur Rylah Institute in conjunction with scientists from major universities, was completed for the Victorian government in June 2025.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/10/victorias-koalas-in-chronically-poor-health-and-population-is-half-what-was-previously-estimated\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-09T20:23:27"
    }
